# SYNTHETIC fixture (T3 fixture #9, design SS5/SS6). HTTP 503 + Retry-After -> RATE_LIMITED.
# Not observed live (site-survey's 26 requests hit 0 rate-limit signals, SS8); shape modeled
# on the generic HttpClient error-mapping table (http.py), same convention as
# tests/fixtures/arxiv/raw/06_oai_503_retry_after.http and
# tests/fixtures/openreview/08_ratelimit_429.http. Custom .http format (fixtures README):
# '#' lines are comments; 'HTTP-STATUS: <int>' gives the status; remaining 'Key: Value' lines
# are response headers; the first blank line separates headers from the raw body -- headers
# are persisted alongside the body so the Retry-After signal round-trips.
HTTP-STATUS: 503
Retry-After: 90
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

<h1>Service Temporarily Unavailable</h1>
